  <div class="foot"><span class="wordmark">Promp<span class="t">T</span><span class="u">ugal</span><i>.news</i></span><span>The industry</span></div>
</section>
<!-- 8 · a service, paid after the value -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="head"><span><b>From product to service</b></span><span>08</span></div>
  <div class="kicker">The unit of news changes, and so does the way it is paid for</div>
  <h2 style="font-size:64px">An article is written once. A maintained claim, kept current, is a service.</h2>
  <div class="vs" style="margin-top:36px">
    <div class="side old" style="padding:30px 36px">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:6px">An article</h3>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 720 190" width="720" height="190">
        <path d="M0,170 L30,24 C110,30 150,128 300,154 S600,166 720,167 L720,170 Z" fill="#f8e4df"/>
        <path d="M0,170 L30,24 C110,30 150,128 300,154 S600,166 720,167" fill="none" stroke="#c52830" stroke-width="4"/>
        <line x1="0" y1="170" x2="720" y2="170" stroke="#121317" stroke-width="2"/>
        <text x="62" y="30" font-size="21" fill="#121317" font-weight="600">published</text>
        <text x="430" y="140" font-size="21" fill="#3f424a">then it goes stale</text>
        <text x="720" y="188" text-anchor="end" class="mono" font-size="18" fill="#595c64">TIME &#8594;</text>
      </svg>
      <p class="body" style="font-size:23px;margin-top:6px">Sold once, by the page or the bundle. Its price is going to zero.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mid">&#8594;</div>
    <div class="side new" style="padding:30px 36px">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:6px;color:#006600">A maintained claim</h3>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 720 190" width="720" height="190">
        <path d="M0,60 H170 V44 H360 V52 H540 V34 H720 V170 H0 Z" fill="#e2eedf"/>
        <path d="M0,60 H170 V44 H360 V52 H540 V34 H720" fill="none" stroke="#006600" stroke-width="4"/>
        <line x1="0" y1="170" x2="720" y2="170" stroke="#121317" stroke-width="2"/>
        <g font-size="20" fill="#3f424a" text-anchor="middle"><circle cx="170" cy="52" r="9" fill="#006600"/><text x="170" y="100">updated</text>
        <circle cx="360" cy="48" r="9" fill="#006600"/><text x="360" y="100">contradicted</text>
        <circle cx="540" cy="43" r="9" fill="#006600"/><text x="540" y="100">superseded</text></g>
        <text x="720" y="188" text-anchor="end" class="mono" font-size="18" fill="#595c64">TIME &#8594;</text>
      </svg>
      <p class="body" style="font-size:23px;margin-top:6px">Kept current until the story ends: worth more every day it is right.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="flow" style="margin-top:34px">
    <div class="step" style="padding:22px 26px"><div class="n" style="font-size:44px">1</div><h3>A starting credit</h3><p>Read first. No wall, no subscription.</p></div>
    <div class="step" style="padding:22px 26px"><div class="n" style="font-size:44px">2</div><h3>Pence per page</h3><p>Pay for what you read, not for the bundle.</p></div>
    <div class="step" style="padding:22px 26px"><div class="n" style="font-size:44px">3</div><h3>Below zero is fine</h3><p>The balance can go negative: value first.</p></div>
    <div class="step" style="padding:22px 26px;border-color:#006600"><div class="n" style="font-size:44px">4</div><h3>Top up</h3><p>Because you already got the value.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="src" style="margin-top:14px">"Paying after the value" (Dinis Cruz, newsroom.sgit.ai, 14 Oct 2026), live there since 11 Oct 2026; on PrompTugal: the reading meter and card top-up.</div>
  <div class="foot"><span class="wordmark">Promp<span class="t">T</span><span class="u">ugal</span><i>.news</i></span><span>The industry</span></div>
</section>
<!-- 9 · provenance -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="head"><span><b>Provenance</b></span><span>09</span></div>
  <div class="kicker">What makes news worth paying for: you can check it</div>
  <h2 style="font-size:66px">The story is a graph. The article is one projection of it.</h2>
  <div class="cols center" style="grid-template-columns:1060px 1fr;gap:60px;margin-top:30px">
